IO-40: read '-' after ')' as a subtraction in math expressions

getOperand() folds a '-' followed by a digit into a negative number when the
previous lexeme is an operator or '(' (codes <= 6, or '^'), but code 2 in
that range is ')'. "(TSS)-1" therefore became "(TSS)" followed by the number
-1 and was rejected as an invalid expression (ERROR 233), while "(TSS) - 1"
parsed. Exclude ')' from the set.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-40_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
index c39dff7..2ea85c4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ int getOperand()
       case '-': code = 4;
         if (Pos < Len-1 &&
             isDigit(S[Pos+1]) &&
-            (CurLex <= 6 || CurLex == 31))
+            ((CurLex <= 6 && CurLex != 2) || CurLex == 31))
         {
             Pos++;
             Fvalue = -getNumber();
